---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"log\"])"
---
The pad's log of its last 64 events, live (needs control channel v1.8 of the gamepadii firmware).

The events are boots, firmware panics, commands, profile changes, saves and restarts. A soft reboot keeps the log; a power-on starts a new one.

Usage: gamepadii log [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

      --from <N>
          Start at this sequence number. Default: the oldest record

      --follow
          Read the log again every 500 ms and show only the new records, until Ctrl-C or until the pad goes away. JSON: one line for each read

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
